-- statement:
--   This block builds a C*-algebraic framework and packages three defined propositions, none asserted as established theorems. For a type ι and normed space H, HilbertSum ι H is the ℓ² sum of copies of H. For a group G, left(g) is the unitary-type operator on ℓ²(G,H) translating coordinates, (left g x)(h)=x(g⁻¹h), with left 1 = 1, left(gh)=left g·left h and adjoint left g⁻¹; diagonal(T) applies a bounded operator T in every coordinate. Algebra(G) is the norm closure of the star algebra generated by the left translations on ℓ²(G,ℂ), a reduced group C*-algebra, with generator(g) the element for g, and F2 is the free group on two generators. For a *-homomorphism ρ from a C*-algebra A to bounded operators on a Hilbert space H, tensorAlgebra(ρ) is the C*-algebra generated by the diagonal copies of ρ(A) together with the left translations. A OneQuasitrace on A is a ℂ-valued map τ with τ(x*x) ≥ 0, τ(x*x)=τ(xx*), additivity τ(h+ik)=τ(h)+iτ(k) on self-adjoint h,k, and linearity on every closed commutative non-unital star subalgebra; it is Normalized if τ(1)=1, and IsTwo if it extends to a one-quasitrace on 2×2 matrices over A whose upper-left-corner values recover τ. ProperlyInfinite A means there are s,t with s*s=1, t*t=1 and s*t=0. ClosedStarIdeal is a norm-closed two-sided star ideal, CStarSimple means every such ideal is zero or everything, StablyFinite means every n×n matrix v over A with v*v=1 also has vv*=1, and TracialState is a positive normalized tracial linear functional. TraceFreeStablyFinite asks for a nontrivial separable stably finite C*-algebra with no tracial state. ReducedQuasitraceLoss asks for a nontrivial separable B with a normalized 2-quasitrace and a faithful representation ρ such that tensorAlgebra over F2 is properly infinite and has no normalized 2-quasitrace. SimpleStableTensorCounterexample asserts that Algebra(F2) is simple and stably finite, and that there is a nontrivial simple stably finite M with a faithful representation whose F2 tensor algebra is properly infinite. StableFinitenessBundle is the conjunction of all three.
